Personal Development (PD) focuses on preparing pupils for their adult lives by teaching them how to engage with society and providing them with ample opportunities to do so (Ofsted Inspection Handbook, July 2022, paragraph 292).
At Cold Aston Primary School, Personal Development is centered on nurturing the whole child to help them reach their full potential academically, socially, emotionally, and spiritually. Our goal is for all pupils to grow into well-educated, respectful, and responsible adults who are:
Comfortable with who they are and have a deep sense of belonging
Respectful of others, viewing differences as positive rather than threatening
Capable of making positive contributions to school life, the wider community, and society in general
Happy, safe, confident, and resilient
Model citizens prepared for life in modern Britain
Cold Aston Primary School teaches personal development in a wide range of ways throughout the children’s school lives. For example:
it is taught in discrete lessons through our PSHE curriculum
it is taught with cross-curricular links in other lessons, such as English, physical education and religious education;
staff members consistently model how to be a good citizen who uphold the school values;
assemblies (whole school and special visitors);
e-Safety lessons in computing and assembly;
celebrating positive learning attributes with weekly certificates;
array of after school clubs;
focusing on mental and physical health;
celebrating different languages, cultures and religions;
outdoor activity trips.
